[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. It holds two problems.
The reports were merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and every subject says "wrong day", so two causes ended up in one ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is a parser fix. It closes only the first row below. The second keeps
coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

Counted from the ticket export, one report per id: the export pages overlap, so some reports
come twice. A report is placed by its tenant and the way it came in (`causes.ts`), not by the
intake tag, which is a guess from the reporter's browser.

## The two problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day
first, so their dates come out with day and month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. It reaches
people through the app, email and the booking-v2 form. This is the bug #4471 describes, and
the queued fix is for it. A few of these reports read as a date moved by one day
(`desk-notes.json`); by tenant they are `parser`, and they are counted there.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first.** The form prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. People do
what the hint says, and the date flips. It comes only through the form, only for the tenants
on booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it: the fix is the hint (or the form's reading),
in booking-v3.

## For the desk

- Keep #4471 for `parser`. Move the `hint` reports to a ticket of their own.
- When the parser fix ships, form reports from booking-v3 tenants that keep coming are `hint`,
  not a failed fix.
- Merging on subject alone put two causes in one ticket. Check the cause before you merge.

